<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: #333;
      max-width: 600px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 20px;
    }
    ul {
      padding-left: 20px;
      margin-top: 5px;
    }
    li {
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .signature {
      margin-top: 30px;
      border-top: 1px solid #ddd;
      padding-top: 20px;
    }
    .signature-name {
      font-weight: bold;
      font-size: 1.1em;
      margin-bottom: 5px;
    }
    .signature-details {
      color: #666;
      font-size: 0.95em;
    }
    .signature-details a {
      color: #4A90E2;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .signature-details a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <p>Dear <%= @organization.name.titleize %> Leadership,</p>

  <p>I am writing to inquire about small, discretionary educational sponsorships for high-performing working adults.</p>

  <p>I am a nontraditional student who has spent the last seven years working full-time in leadership roles to self-fund my education. As of <strong>October 17, 2025,</strong> I was accepted into the <strong>Bachelor of Business Leadership</strong> program at the University of Massachusetts Global<strong>.</strong></p>

  <p><strong>The Situation:</strong><br>
  While I am working additional shifts to cover the majority of my tuition, the cost of required course materials, textbooks, and student fees creates a recurring coverage gap that can delay progress if left unaddressed.</p>

  <p><strong>The Ask:</strong><br>
  I am not seeking a large scholarship. I am reaching out to community organizations for <strong>micro-grants of $25–$100</strong> to help cover specific educational line items such as books or technology fees. Even small contributions compound quickly and allow me to continue my studies without interruption.</p>

  <p><strong>Why I Am a Safe Investment:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Top 1% Performance:</strong> Recipient of the <strong>Disney Legacy Award,</strong> granted to fewer than <strong>1% of 1%</strong> of Disney Cast Members globally</li>
    <li><strong>Academic Consistency: 3.5 GPA</strong> maintained while balancing full-time (often 50+ hour) leadership roles</li>
    <li><strong>Service:</strong> Active volunteer with <strong>Fisher House Foundation</strong> and <strong>Toys for Tots,</strong> with a strong respect for the stewardship of community dollars</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Transparency & Verification:</strong><br>
  All contributions are directed exclusively to a verified <strong>529 Education Savings Plan</strong> and used strictly for educational expenses. Rather than attaching documents, I’ve made my academic and professional summary available here:<br>
  <a href="https://johannalucilleroberts.com" target="_blank">johannalucilleroberts.com</a></p>

  <p>If your organization supports individuals who demonstrate grit, leadership, and long-term community return<strong>,</strong> I would be grateful for your consideration.</p>

  <p><em><strong>Let’s go the distance.</strong></em></p>

  <p><strong>Respectfully,</strong></p>

  <div class="signature">
    <div class="signature-name">Johanna Lucille Roberts</div>
    <div class="signature-details">
      <a href="https://johannalucilleroberts.com" target="_blank">johannalucilleroberts.com</a><br>
      Support my education: <a href="https://connect.vestwell.com/gift/oregon-college/1byH4tqvzE2-akObncIe9A" target="_blank">Oregon College Savings Plan</a><br>
      8482 SW Jessica St. Unit 1702<br>
      Wilsonville, OR 97070
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>